case <-stop: return
case <-ctx.Done(): return
case jobs <- i:
}
```

But note: after sending jobs <- i, the worker has taken it and will execute fn even after ctx is cancelled — that's fine, "wait for running calls to return". fn receives ctx so it should observe cancellation. In practice fn might not check ctx but the contract assumes cooperative fn.

Workers:
```go
